==Portuguese==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|pt|accordar||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|pt|roa-opt|acordar}}, from {{inh|pt|VL.|*accordāre}}. Sense of "to wake up" was possibly influenced by {{inh|pt|la|cordatus||wise, prudent}}<ref>https://www.dicio.com.br/acordar/</ref>, which would yield *cordado if inherited.

===Pronunciation===
{{pt-IPA}}
* {{hyphenation|pt|a|cor|dar}}

===Verb===
{{pt-verb}}

# {{senseid|pt|to gain consciousness}} {{lb|pt|intransitive}} to [[awake]]; to [[wake up]] {{gloss|to stop sleeping}}
#: {{uxi|pt|'''Acordei''' às sete da manhã.|'''I woke up''' at seven in the morning.}}
#: {{syn|pt|despertar<qq:more formal>}}
#: {{ant|pt|adormecer|cair no sono|dormir}}
# {{senseid|pt|to cause to wake up}} {{lb|pt|transitive}} to [[wake]]; to [[wake up]]; to [[awaken]] {{gloss|to cause someone to stop sleeping}}
#* {{RQ:mul:Rowling Harry Potter|pt-BR|3|page=336|text=Francamente, vão '''acordar''' todo mundo!|t=Honestly, you're going '''to wake''' everyone '''up'''!}}
#: {{uxi|pt|Não faça barulho, senão pode '''acordar''' os vizinhos.|Don’t make noise, or you could '''wake''' the neighbours '''up'''.}}
#: {{syn|pt|despertar<qq:more formal>}}
#: {{ant|pt|ninar}}
# {{senseid|pt|to become aware of a serious issue}} {{indtr|pt|para|intr=1}} to [[wake up]] (to) {{gloss|to become aware of a serious issue}}
#: {{uxi|pt|O país inteiro '''acorda''' para o terrorismo.|The whole country is '''waking up''' to [the problem of] terrorism.}}
#: {{syn|pt|despertar}}
# {{senseid|pt|to stop being sleepy}} {{lb|pt|intransitive}} to [[wake up]] {{gloss|to stop being sleepy}}
#: {{uxi|pt|Tomei um café para '''acordar'''.|I drank some coffee to '''wake myself up'''.}}
# {{senseid|pt|to cause to stop being sleepy}} {{lb|pt|transitive}} to [[wake up]] {{gloss|to cause to stop being sleepy}}
#: {{uxi|pt|Só um energético consegue me '''acordar'''.|Only an energy drink can '''wake''' me '''up'''.}}
# {{senseid|pt|to arouse}} {{lb|pt|transitive}} to [[instigate]]; to [[stir up]] {{gloss|to incite feelings}}
#: {{uxi|pt|Os eventos '''acordaram''' a raiva dos franceses.|The events '''stirred up''' the anger of the French.}}
#: {{syn|pt|instigar}}
# {{senseid|pt|to accord}} {{lb|pt|transitive}} to [[accord]] {{gloss|to bring into accord}}
#: {{uxi|pt|Os inimigos tiveram que '''acordar''' suas diferenças.|The enemies had to '''accord''' their differences.}}
#: {{syn|pt|concordar|harmonizar}}

